Description: SecuBox Jellyfin — LXC-native media server (MIND layer)
 Runs Jellyfin in a Debian bookworm LXC at 10.100.0.170 on br-lxc, behind the
 SecuBox chain (HAProxy TLS 1.3 → sbxwaf → nginx). Replaces the earlier
 Docker/Podman-based 1.0.0 host-API stub with the peertube/lyrion LXC model.
 .
 The unprivileged host API (/api/v1/jellyfin/, JWT-gated) delegates every
 privileged action to the audited root helper jellyfinctl over scoped sudo:
 LXC start/stop/restart, library scans, and Jellyfin/version upgrades.
 .
 Partner auto-wire detects the sibling SecuBox media services (photoprism,
 nextcloud, torrent, lyrion) by the presence of their media directory and
 read-only bind-mounts each into the Jellyfin LXC as a virtual-folder library
 (peertube stays a deep link). Wiring is independently toggleable per partner.
